  "prefLabel": "Agr 904.07 Tolerances for Established Grades",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-02-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 904.07 Tolerances for Established Grades. In order to allow for variations incident to proper grading and handling, not more than 10 percent by count of the packaged maple syrup in any lot shall have syrup below the requirements for the grade, provided:\n\n(a) There shall be no damage;\n\n(b) None of the syrup shall be darker than the color standard than that which is required of the next darker grade;\n\n(c) None of the syrup shall be lighter than the color standard than that which is required of the next lighter grade; and\n\n(d) None of the syrup shall be outside the range of density identified in Agr 904.04.\n\nSource. #6453, eff 2-15-97, EXPIRED: 2-15-05\n\nNew. #10744, eff 12-16-14 (from Agr 904.06); ss by #14225, eff 3-29-25 (formerly Agr 904.06)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html"
